Dual Authentication Strategy for DX Dataplane
--------------------------------------------

Document set:
1) Strategy and Decisions (this file)
2) HTTP Rich-Context Approach (http-rich-context.doc)
3) HTTP Token-Exchange Approach (http-token-exchange.doc)
4) gRPC Rich-Context Approach (grpc-rich-context.doc)
5) Open Questions Checklist (open-questions.doc)

Purpose
Provide implementation-ready guidance to support both JWT and AppId/AppSecret (or AppId-only) authentication on the dataplane, with clear options for HTTP and gRPC links to the controlplane, trade-offs, and decision points.

Key goals
- Allow clients to call dataplane with either Bearer JWT or app credentials (AppId +/- AppSecret).
- Keep downstream authorization logic unchanged wherever possible.
- Ensure service-to-service calls from dataplane to controlplane are authenticated and efficient.

Recommended default
- Use Rich-Context verification (no JWT minting) over HTTP (or gRPC if infra ready).

Contents
- See the per-approach docs listed above for flow, sequence diagrams (text), data contracts, and rollout steps.

